				id: "D8414AB6A86181F6"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "How progression works"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["E60381A75A8C4D21"]
			description: [
				"ItemStages enforces item and namespace access where that is technically reliable. It does not pretend to stop mobs from spawning, block exploration systems, or gate every world mechanic."
				""
				"Normal production quests only detect their listed items. Promotion contracts, Market Orders, and shop purchases explicitly consume their listed inputs, so read the task before handing over scarce goods."
				""
				"A Bounty Board uses the inserted decree to choose a level-specific order pool. If a decree is lost, the Replacement Decrees chapter sells another after that level is unlocked; buying one does not advance your level."
			]
			icon: "kubejs:copper_coin"
